The /javaagent.jar payload is rebuilt from official v2.33.1 source commit
d9045e02e0711837d54f0fd058cd55f77742506d with the Elven-reviewed
jedis4-terminal-error.patch. This is a PATCHED artifact, not an unchanged
upstream agent. The original copy utility, image entrypoint and notices remain.
The patch propagates a synchronous Jedis4 method's actual terminal Throwable
to the existing client span and preserves the earlier send-command Throwable
when no terminal Throwable exists. It creates no additional spans. The common
no-argument method remains available for unmodified older Jedis callers.
Upstream reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20792
